What is the output of following C program?

#include <stdio.h>
main() {
    int i,j,x=0;
    for (i=0; i<5; ++i)
        for (j=0; j<i; ++j) {
            x += (i+j-1);
            break;
        }
    printf("%d",x);
}

Which of the following are legal statements in C programming language?

(A) int *P = &44;
(B) int *P = &r;
(C) int P = &a;
(D) int P = a;
